.TH RFID-COMMANDS 1 "2026-07-28" "GWAY local tools" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
rfid-commands \- overview of local RFID scan and command tools
.SH DESCRIPTION
The local RFID command system has three main layers:
.PP
.B rfid-scan-publisher
owns the RC522 hardware and writes passive scan state.
.PP
.B rfid-mode-runner
watches the scan file and interprets
.I /home/arthe/.config/rfid-modes/cards
as a card-driven state machine.
.PP
.B rfid-register
creates directories and scripts in that state tree.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
/home/arthe/.local/bin/rfid-register --list
/home/arthe/.local/bin/rfid-mode-runner --status
/home/arthe/.local/bin/rfid-register --latest --dir
/home/arthe/.local/bin/rfid-register --path FIRST_CARD --wait --command 'date >> /home/arthe/rfid-runs.log'
/home/arthe/.local/bin/rfid-mode-runner --once --dry-run
systemctl status rfid-scan-publisher.service --no-pager
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /home/arthe/.local/state/rfid-mode/rfid-scan.json
Latest local RFID scan state.
.TP
.I /home/arthe/.config/rfid-modes/cards
Card state tree and command scripts.
.TP
.I /home/arthe/.config/rfid-modes/logs/events.ndjson
Mode-runner event log.
.SH SAFETY
Do not put secrets in card scripts. Do not bind unknown cards to destructive
commands. Avoid overwriting high-value cards unless that replacement is
explicitly intended.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR rfid-register (1),
.BR rfid-mode-runner (1),
.BR rfid-scan-publisher (1),
.BR rfid-clear-current (1)
